gpu/buddy: honour top-down in the fallback to the other free tree

alloc_from_freetree searches top-down (get_maxblock) only in the tree the
request names: the clear tree for a GPU_BUDDY_CLEAR_ALLOCATION. When that
tree has no block of the order, it falls back to the other tree with the
plain smallest-order scan, dropping GPU_BUDDY_TOPDOWN_ALLOCATION. amdgpu's
KFD VRAM BOs are VRAM_CLEARED and top-down: with the clear tree empty they
landed in the low VRAM, the CPU-visible window of a small-BAR card (245 of
256 MiB held by one compute process with over 13 GB free), so every
CPU-access allocation had to evict them. The fallback now searches the
other tree top-down when top-down was asked for.

Drop this patch when the pin picks up the dirty-tracker rework of the
buddy allocator ("gpu/buddy: replace dual-tree/force_merge with a
decoupled dirty tracker"), which removes the separate trees.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/buddy.c b/drivers/gpu/buddy.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/buddy.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/buddy.c
@@ -820,11 +820,17 @@ alloc_from_freetree(struct gpu_buddy *mm,
 		tree = (tree == GPU_BUDDY_CLEAR_TREE) ?
 			GPU_BUDDY_DIRTY_TREE : GPU_BUDDY_CLEAR_TREE;
 
-		for (tmp = order; tmp <= mm->max_order; ++tmp) {
-			root = &mm->free_trees[tree][tmp];
-			block = rbtree_last_free_block(root);
+		if (flags & GPU_BUDDY_TOPDOWN_ALLOCATION) {
+			block = get_maxblock(mm, order, tree);
 			if (block)
-				break;
+				tmp = gpu_buddy_block_order(block);
+		} else {
+			for (tmp = order; tmp <= mm->max_order; ++tmp) {
+				root = &mm->free_trees[tree][tmp];
+				block = rbtree_last_free_block(root);
+				if (block)
+					break;
+			}
 		}
 
 		if (!block)
